+## What the DomA features are for
+
+Where an item relies on changes outside this repository, it says so. The SoDeV
+Raspberry Pi workspace that builds this product
+(`automotive-grade-linux/sodev-demo-workspace-rpi`) carries those changes as
+patches against other AOSP projects and the guest kernel, and applies them to
+the checkout.
+
+* **Vulkan compositing.** `BOARD_MESA3D_VULKAN_DRIVERS := virtio` builds the Venus ICD
+  and `PRODUCT_PACKAGES += vulkan.virtio` installs it (the board config only defines the
+  module; an unasked-for module is never installed),
+  `ro.hardware.vulkan=virtio` makes the loader look for it, and
+  `TARGET_VULKAN_SUPPORT := false` drops `com.google.cf.vulkan` -- whose `.rc` sets
+  `ro.vulkan.apex`, which confines the loader's search to that APEX's linker namespace
+  and would hide an ICD in `/vendor`. `debug.renderengine.backend=skiavkthreaded` and
+  `debug.hwui.renderer=skiavk` then move SurfaceFlinger and HWUI onto it. Without all
+  six the guest runs on the Venus device line and still composites with GL, and the
+  difference is only run-to-run noise -- which is what made the missing switch look like
+  Venus doing nothing.
+* **Wi-Fi, shadow AP.** The guest gets simulated radios that beacon the SSIDs
+  the host really sees, so the AAOS Wi-Fi screen lists real access points
+  instead of virt_wifi's single synthetic entry; `DomaWifiRelay` is what makes
+  an access point the seed file does not list connectable, because it is the
+  only component that can see the passphrase the user typed. The radios need
+  `mac80211_hwsim` in the guest kernel's module set, which the workspace adds,
+  and the scan results and the real association come from DomD.
+* **Bluetooth A2DP.** The audio policy fork names the Bluetooth audio module
+  that AOSP 17 actually ships, without which media routes "successfully" while
+  nothing comes out of the speaker. It also relies on the workspace's patch to
+  `packages/modules/Bluetooth` and on the HCI transport DomD provides.
+* **Bluetooth HFP.** Software-datapath SCO plus the dialer the product really
+  installs, without which an incoming call rings inside Telecom with no screen
+  and no ringtone. It also relies on the workspace's patches to
+  `packages/modules/Bluetooth`, `frameworks/base` and `packages/services/Car`.
+* **Hardware decode.** Behind `XT_DOMA_HWDEC=true`: the V4L2 Codec2 service over
+  the host's video decoder, reached through virtio-media, with the seccomp
+  policy it needs. The service's sepolicy, the `external/v4l2_codec2`
+  namespace and the SurfaceFlinger frame-rate property are in every build.
+  It also relies on the workspace's patch to
+  `external/v4l2_codec2`, on the virtio-media driver in the guest kernel, and on
+  a DomA device model that provides a virtio-media device.
 
